I'm curious to know, who are you?

I think the Lojban community is now different right down to its core than i=
t
was eight years ago. The degree to which it is a "project" is beginning to
be outstripped by the degree to which it is a language. I guess back then
people joined up in order to have the kind of conversation John and xorxes
are having. Now, many of us are joining to make podcasts and webcomics and
horror novels, and don't really give a darn about that other stuff. It is
leaving the stage where the project is to develop the language, and enterin=
g
the stage where the project is to spread the language and accumulate a huge
corpus of texts.
-epkat
           
